# The vault is its own repository.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, which is load-bearing. A bare `vault/` matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, and this app has `app/api/vault/` - so the two
# route files that serve every project read and write were silently untracked. `git
# status` said clean, the app ran fine locally, and a clone was missing its API.
/vault/

.env*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
.groundwork-e2e/
